R-CH8 R-CH9 R-NS2 R-NS3 R-NS4 R-CH11 (slice 240, Design Q615 item 5): `nightly = false` in config.toml. A bare name is `reify@latest`, and the switch applies to `@latest` (R-NS3) with a user build as a nightly (R-CH9): `tln roc install reify --yes` is exit 10 (kind no_tuple), nothing is installed. An id is a name of the user (R-NS4): `tln roc install reify-2026-11-03-1708298 --yes` installs. The text of the exit 10 failure is a proposal (TW24, accepted 2026-11-10 for the form of R-NS2: the switch and its source). The calls.log lines are a guess: the list is read before the domain is known to be empty.
